{title: Your Heart Is My Home}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
Arranged by Deborah Johnson
Copyright (C) 1997 Lawrence Keith Holder

Verse 2
1. Your heart is my home, wherever I am;
Never alone will I be,
For tho' I be near, or tho' I be far,
It is you bringing sunlight to me.

Verse 3
2. Your heart is my home, tho' I sail the seas
Where the course may change with the wind.
Like the stars that guide a ship in the night,
I find joy in the love that you send.

Verse 4
(Bridge)
The highways, they lead to a thousand places,
But so often, the road's all I see.
Tho' I run to the mountains, or take to the valley,
Your heart is still home to me...

Verse 5
3. Your heart is my home, wherever I am,
Like the sun shining through all the rain.
I know if I go, I must surely return,
Just to know you are with me again.
